#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1080.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167890} :activity/id #uuid "18df0fdd-60be-5a81-a0cd-e95103dfb1c0" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049896 :topic/id #uuid "1c8e94f0-f686-5ab0-b88e-99e6f26eaf54" :topic/math-academy-id 3232} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167886 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167982 :tutorial/content "![](images/44/44a90d0fa61d3643848f01479706cca752a00914b99185da5b8739c5e1cab182.svg)\n\n**Step 1**. In the initial value problem above, we apply the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation.\n\nFirst, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{5{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=5L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+6L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+3=5{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=-2{X}_{1}(s)+6{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$\n\n**Step 2**. Now, solving the first equation for $X_1(s),$ we get\n\n$$\ns X_1(s) +  3 = 5 X_1(s)\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nX_1(s) = -\\dfrac{3}{s-5}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for $X_2(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns X_2(s) -  2 = -2\\left(-\\dfrac{3}{s-5}\\right) + 6 X_2(s) \n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\dfrac{2s-4}{(s-5)(s-6)}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**. To find $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to $X_1(s)$ and $X_2(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{-\\frac{3}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =-3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{5t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2s-4}{(s-5)(s-6)}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{8}{s-6}-\\frac{6}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =8{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-6}\\}-6{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =8{e}^{6t}-6{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3{e}^{5t} \\\\ 8{e}^{6t}-6{e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{6t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "a475ed27-9529-52d2-85cb-9e8827c5b45e" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14201 :tutorial/title "A Worked Example"} :step/id #uuid "648d1a99-8c25-5200-8b95-382792dca052" :step/math-academy-id 590676 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167887}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167887 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166930 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166510 :question/id #uuid "0b2a74d8-1ce2-5055-a843-1456b1878cf7" :question/math-academy-id "e-21157"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd7b8fc8-26d3-5551-9a46-45725bd863a6" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048605} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050098}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167162} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167206} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304952} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304953} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304954} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390939} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390955} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433217} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433219}] :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Laplace Transform to a System of Linear ODEs"} :step/id #uuid "887d1a2a-3793-57e6-a390-bcc123897754" :step/math-academy-id 590677 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167888}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167888 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166931 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166508 :question/id #uuid "d9715a0c-6808-5db8-b0b4-5bedc4f2e9e8" :question/math-academy-id "e-21155"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c81626a0-6613-5f5d-9dda-df853958c571" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167159} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167163} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304955} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304957} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304958} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304963} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433218} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507441} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507462} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507519}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"} :step/id #uuid "c39529f2-6303-5dd8-a113-cdaf40a5d673" :step/math-academy-id 590680 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167889}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167889 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166932 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166509 :question/id #uuid "ec8e6fde-504e-581f-b465-6a9bc3927d77" :question/math-academy-id "e-21156"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050768}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167160} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167161} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305033} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305034} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305035} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305036} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305037} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459218} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459220} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507472}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"} :step/id #uuid "aa736c0f-1eaa-5601-a02e-62159a1f73b2" :step/math-academy-id 590683} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167890 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168031 :tutorial/content "In this topic, we'll learn how to use Laplace transforms to solve homogeneous systems like the one below.\n![](images/66/66eb9ce1b87b67ba550fc0b76493b775bf2b2e67be257b9fe9974db9d53cdffa.svg)\n\nThe process can be split into three steps.\n\n- **Step 1.** Apply the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation, to get a system with variables \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\} \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Solve the obtained system for variables \n\n$$\nX_1(s) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s).\n$$\n\n- **Step 3.** To find the initial variables\n\n$$\nx_1(t) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad x_2(t)\n$$\n\nsatisfying the original initial value problem, apply the inverse Laplace transform to \n\n$$\nX_1(s) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s).\n$$\n\nLet's see how this works in practice." :tutorial/id #uuid "98573e3a-ebcd-565e-8de7-a83e3deb9d09" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14610 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "f663bde1-a39c-5d4d-83fd-15b833a5cbea" :step/math-academy-id 590687 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167886}}] :activity/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186167006}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459336} :activity/id #uuid "ba53db0c-7cf4-5014-beca-52ff11bcbf37" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049896 :topic/id #uuid "1c8e94f0-f686-5ab0-b88e-99e6f26eaf54" :topic/math-academy-id 3232} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459312 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305037 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3db932f4-fae5-50c6-9f86-537475346704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302842}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302842} :answer-field/id #uuid "51f9ccbb-98c5-5a7d-8a34-9b6a924b104f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304304} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3ce928a-a5a9-5225-8c9f-2f61190156c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303464}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303464} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b95b873-f263-55a4-aa11-176bdc917560" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304494} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b600c94-694f-5df9-8995-92f0759d4e67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303219}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303219} :answer-field/id #uuid "a99db976-4eb3-54c9-b026-70c5ab583549" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304540} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c87bd0e-68f0-53c0-a1da-53a949f4133b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303021}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303021} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee8a77b9-f4f3-5da7-a356-159e03040e12" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304720}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "317fc248-dee8-522d-9f3a-ce7380dbab1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-332439" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-5{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{4}{s-6},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{5}{s}-\\frac{4}{s-6}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n$x(t)=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n$\\,\\,+\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n$\\,\\,{e}^{6t}$\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-3}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-4}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{4}{s-6}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+4{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-6}\\} \\\\  & =1+4{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =1+4{e}^{6t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{5}{s}-\\frac{4}{s-6}\\} \\\\  & =5{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}-4{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-6}\\} \\\\  & =5-4{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =5-4{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+4{e}^{6t} \\\\ 5-4{e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0904e369-cbe5-5cae-826c-aebc85ee57b8"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459315 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459218 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8489f83-40a0-5fa2-86f5-bd04c15c744a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459034}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459034} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f1fd3da-f4de-532f-a46e-f3ecb6847ac3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459097} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a6d7c96-1bca-5bf1-899f-bcc0cdc4ebc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458712}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186458712} :answer-field/id #uuid "282aaf72-408c-5f10-8ec6-186aa6a44cdc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459102} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec06874d-7f4b-520f-b784-c3ff1e8d0cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459043}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459043} :answer-field/id #uuid "346e7d15-351c-5545-950d-eeabcb321de2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459109} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "338cd1b7-92b2-52a0-8bfb-86cc6a89733e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458727}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186458727} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e028d21-3f7c-5da7-8e50-d18b331f55cd" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "26b8e713-769d-5a04-9ac2-84441f94ba94" :question/math-academy-id "q-332395" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{3}{s}+\\frac{2}{s-3},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{3t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{3}{s}+\\frac{2}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+2{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =3+2{e}^{3t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1-{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =3-{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3+2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 3-{e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1867188e-5193-5fba-a25c-9cda18c82e06" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459312}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459324 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304958 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95d1ef6b-caf6-5764-bc12-294fa204246c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{-4s-17}{(s-4)(s+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303387}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303387} :answer-field/id #uuid "518f0276-0f4b-5c49-a892-c180fc62763c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304299} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee8ef59c-2d4f-5cd8-bd73-bde62a85dcd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{s+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303953}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303953} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdcc71fe-ab2d-5096-8ba2-82ce4b706e91" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304592}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0c4c84fb-7fb4-580a-bff4-417ed1ebd433" :question/math-academy-id "q-331918" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3=-2{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+4=-3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get \n\n$$\ns{X}_{1}(s)-3=-2{X}_{1}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3}{s+2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s)$ gives\n\n$$\ns{X}_{2}(s)+4=-3(\\frac{3}{s+2})+4{X}_{2}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-4s-17}{(s-4)(s+2)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4eee263e-af64-5d11-8a4c-803224d75fa4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459331}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459331 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459220 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09ce315d-395c-57f6-9266-37e8d3f8b69c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458636}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186458636} :answer-field/id #uuid "3facc676-db7c-504b-ad37-cb6479ec45aa" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459119} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca4efff0-ed8b-5efd-baf0-8bedffbf9612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458986}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186458986} :answer-field/id #uuid "4970ea8c-d3ed-5408-b30d-972d0f9f7a39" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459122} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "184e26b8-c664-56cb-af6b-ea4090d916b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458668}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186458668} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8864a88-2dcd-5b4e-a2d6-71c37f0f4d96" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459157} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b34ae040-bdf3-5b46-a211-b8e15b7220a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458951}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186458951} :answer-field/id #uuid "af20bb90-cb1f-52c6-b8c0-17deb5f81cee" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2e221fc3-b674-5d25-8035-e02c5aeade93" :question/math-academy-id "q-332300" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{5}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{5}{s-2}+\\frac{2}{s+1}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{2t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{-t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{5}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =5\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =5{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =5{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{5}{s-2}+\\frac{2}{s+1}\\} \\\\  & =5\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}+2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s+1}\\} \\\\  & =5{e}^{2\\cdot t}+2{e}^{-1\\cdot t} \\\\  & =5{e}^{2t}+2{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5{e}^{2t} \\\\ 5{e}^{2t}+2{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b198a7e9-9895-5cae-a9de-bc7b16a22973" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459315}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459336 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167159 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c50b2be-602c-50a5-ab71-1319601cdfad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2-3s}{(s-1)(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458764}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186458764} :answer-field/id #uuid "faed85bb-89ce-5a06-b08b-d84b4c3cd7a9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164004} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75b58a4a-5911-578a-866b-5d33776cf35d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458835}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186458835} :answer-field/id #uuid "18a50378-7dea-5125-b1f1-8186b60315c8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164005}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "17eee175-34bb-5ca1-9aad-a080088cd275" :question/math-academy-id "q-322280" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1={X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+3=-{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\ns{X}_{1}(s)-1={X}_{1}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{1}{s-1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns{X}_{2}(s)+3=-(\\frac{1}{s-1})+3{X}_{2}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-3s+2}{(s-1)(s-3)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d7d523e8-f469-5779-93ad-c004bb0c274f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459324}}] :activity/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458612}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507587} :activity/id #uuid "41eabed7-eb35-5f45-ae65-a1549a8e0311" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049896 :topic/id #uuid "1c8e94f0-f686-5ab0-b88e-99e6f26eaf54" :topic/math-academy-id 3232} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507538 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507441 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0692da6b-ac17-55ad-9bcd-1f26bdf2ad6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2s-5}{(s-2)(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506688}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506688} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0642696-6971-5290-bc2b-f5e549ec1a8d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5aba7ba8-bc90-5a73-9994-754c33e2f759" :question/math-academy-id "q-332038" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3s-8}{(s-2)(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3={X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=-{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-1){X}_{1}(s)-2{X}_{2}(s)=3 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s)+(s-4){X}_{2}(s)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=2-(s-4){X}_{2}(s).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-1)[2-(s-4){X}_{2}(s)]-2{X}_{2}(s) & =3 \\\\ 2(s-1)-[(s-1)(s-4)+2]{X}_{2}(s) & =3 \\\\ -({s}^{2}-5s+6){X}_{2}(s) & =3-2(s-1) \\\\ -(s-2)(s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =-2s+5 \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s-5}{(s-2)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =2-(s-4){X}_{2}(s) \\\\  & =2-(s-4)\\cdot \\frac{2s-5}{(s-2)(s-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(s-2)(s-3)-(s-4)(2s-5)}{(s-2)(s-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3s-8}{(s-2)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3s-8}{(s-2)(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s-5}{(s-2)(s-3)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "20ed4341-142c-5d21-8a9d-5dcc594bddbe" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507560}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507549 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507519 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96a96d60-5df7-525f-b9d5-460b27317666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{s-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507005}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507005} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ea34c0d-6f70-52cb-8ac2-9e4d837fa8f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507313} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b891e4e8-a932-5e13-8640-98de8fa2c1b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{-2s-2}{(s-3)(s-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507085}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507085} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1cf17fd-da35-507f-b449-a0c201f4cbdd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e1650579-5a44-5386-9786-86764c11f1fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-331915" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-4=3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+2=-2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\ns{X}_{1}(s)-4=3{X}_{1}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{4}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns{X}_{2}(s)+2=-2(\\frac{4}{s-3})+{X}_{2}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-2s-2}{(s-1)(s-3)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4f938b5a-9fc6-52bb-ada7-1b71f278f26f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507538}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507560 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507472 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a25cd5e-273b-5e0e-9040-00a8c2d10252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506774}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506774} :answer-field/id #uuid "4baf5e43-602f-5a2a-af70-6e70b13c11b5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507283} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16629947-5e40-577a-9d59-2c4eb055b348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506721}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506721} :answer-field/id #uuid "7225371b-bd06-5f60-a97e-ad353ead8edd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507305} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25cc5a4e-ca9b-57bd-9bdf-37feb9b64059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506763}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506763} :answer-field/id #uuid "9523a40b-2cb7-5f8d-a383-7ba5eb9b0d40" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507333} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cecdaf07-fce9-5488-9f84-191bfeae49d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507127}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507127} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebae569e-81df-5f8a-a1a7-dc127fd41a2e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a3c3395d-f560-5a1d-9156-22f49e61fe66" :question/math-academy-id "q-332290" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{4}{s-4}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{2t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{4t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{4}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}-4{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\cdot t}-4{e}^{4\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}-4{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}-4{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8104dbdf-36d0-5a9c-af1e-91945fd05ed6"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507570 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507462 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31a95984-f3ff-5d40-aa45-92f765a76484" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3s-1}{(s+1)(s-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506796}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506796} :answer-field/id #uuid "35230cec-1558-5848-ab5a-d11ccbfeb44d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507269} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e846976b-6bbf-5002-a11d-4c4ba08add2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{s+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507190}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507190} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6f7f1d9-3783-567e-8823-55b10da69ad9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9a8a2b45-1f2b-5de6-b95b-a5731dcdb607" :question/math-academy-id "q-331914" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{4{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=4L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1=-{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-3=4{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\ns{X}_{1}(s)+1=-{X}_{1}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{1}{s+1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns{X}_{2}(s)-3=4(-\\frac{1}{s+1})+2{X}_{2}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3s-1}{(s+1)(s-2)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b0b567e9-654d-55d5-b9dc-8fd5d056d374" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507549}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507587 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96875261-1814-5e7b-b61f-3304d81295e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507004}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507004} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3dadf3b-7159-55f9-a626-90fba9eed477" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164010} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fa1b31a-f357-5564-b7cd-7e75d306bc93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506793}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506793} :answer-field/id #uuid "c950654f-244e-5514-befa-91dd1f50705b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164011} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca18861d-726a-5a83-b401-6cdb30bef373" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507118}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507118} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbeeb397-fe1f-5065-8997-1a7a9ff96c66" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164012} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94d2d8dc-c36f-51da-9b72-eac13162db91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507002}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507002} :answer-field/id #uuid "22f5e3fa-b810-513c-96f1-e73398a170ae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6b769427-838e-5978-9061-abde5d64f343" :question/math-academy-id "q-322289" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{10}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{5}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{3t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{10}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =10{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =10\\cdot 1-{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =10-{e}^{3t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{5}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =5{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 1+{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =5+{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10-{e}^{3t} \\\\ 5+{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e6ac8913-bf9c-5ca3-8750-bc65c8b2ddd7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507570}}] :activity/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506666}]}
